Short:        Open source WW2 German submarine simulation (Mesa 3D port)
Author:       Thorsten Jordan, Luis Barrancos and others (AmigaOS 4 port by TearsOfMe)
Uploader:     TearsOfMe
Type:         game/sim
Version:      0.3.900-mesa-r3
Architecture: ppc-amigaos >= 4.1.0

================================================================================
                    DANGER FROM THE DEEP (AmigaOS 4.1)
================================================================================

[English version below - Deutsche Version weiter unten]

================================================================================
[EN] ENGLISH
================================================================================

Danger from the Deep (dftd) is an advanced open-source World War II German 
submarine simulation. The game features realistic submarine simulation physics, 
celestial mechanics, convoy behavior, acoustic sensors, torpedo ballistics, 
damage control, and full 3D graphics.

This package provides native, highly optimized AmigaOS 4.1 Mesa 3D builds.

REQUIREMENTS:
- AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition (Update 1 or 2 recommended)
- PowerPC processor (AmigaOne X1000, X5000, A1222+, Sam460, etc.)
- 3D graphics hardware with Warp3D Nova and Mesa 3D (RadeonHD or RadeonRX)
- Minimum 512 MB RAM (1 GB recommended)
- AHI audio system
- Embedded stack cookie: 4 MB ($STACK: 4194304)

INCLUDED EXECUTABLES:
1. DangerFromTheDeep        (WITHOUT DEBUG - RECOMMENDED FOR REGULAR GAMING)
   - Highest performance build with -O3 and AltiVec/VMX optimizations.
   - All debug logging overhead disabled (zero console popups, no file writes).
   - Recommended for daily play.

2. DangerFromTheDeep_Debug  (WITH DEBUG - FOR LOGGING & TROUBLESHOOTING)
   - Diagnostic build with logging enabled.
   - Writes detailed startup and game status to "T:dangerdeep_startup.log".
   - Useful for testing graphics drivers or reporting issues.

INSTALLATION:
Extract the archive to any location on your hard drive (e.g. Work:Games/) and
double-click the "DangerFromTheDeep" icon.
A compatible "mesa.library" is provided in the "libs/" subdirectory for systems
that require it.

KEYBOARD CONTROLS (QUICK REFERENCE):
Stations:
  [F1] Gauges & Helm          [F6] Torpedo Room
  [F2] Periscope              [F7] Damage Control
  [F3] UZO Target Optics      [F8] Logbook / KTB
  [F4] Bridge View            [F9] Sunk Ships Record
  [F5] Navigation Map        [F10] Free Camera

Helm & Throttle:
  [Cursor Left/Right] Rudder Port / Starboard
  [Cursor Up/Down]    Dive planes
  [Return]            Rudder Amidships
  [1]..[4]            Ahead Slow / Half / Flank / Stop
  [5]..[6]            Astern Slow / Full

Diving & Combat:
  [s] Surface                 [0] Raise / Lower Scope
  [p] Periscope Depth         [Space] Lock Target
  [c] Crash Dive (Alarm)      [t] Fire Torpedo
  [d] Snorkel Depth           [g] Deck Gun
  [+] / [-] Map Zoom          [F11] / [F12] Time Compression

Detailed instructions: Please read "MANUAL.txt" (English) or "ANLEITUNG.txt" (German).

